 "verdict": "Scope-(a) constraint analysis for the A>=5 atom->knot rule. (1) The untruncated linear-chain tower is excluded by arithmetic at A>=5 unless Vol_n collapses (required avg volume falls 5.54 -> 1.79 from A=4 to A=6 vs the 7.3-8.3 corpus 3-carriers); with the \u2074He census-gap negative, the single-volume linear-chain reading does not extend. (2) The p^Z n^N ordering leaves ppp/nnn 3-carriers unassigned at A>=5 \u2014 the rule is underdetermined even at n=3 \u2014 though the bracketed n<=3 layer alone spans AME at A=6,7. (3) ALPHA-CLUSTER ADDITIVITY (zero fit, AME-level clusters): the 2-alpha anchor 8Be reproduces AME to +0.16%; one-bond composites undershoot mildly (6Li -4.61%, 7Li -6.29%, 9Be -2.70%); multi-bond composites degrade (11B -14.6%, 14N -16.8%, 19F -17.7%). Additivity is a consistent LOWER BOUND (all deficits > 0 except the famously 2alpha-unbound 8Be) whose deficit is the inter-cluster bond term; the implied per-bond volumes (2.9 -> 12.8, guarded) are NON-CONSTANT, so the missing term is not one universal volume. This constrains the composite rule class as-is; it does not exclude the composite ingredient (permanence principle: the cluster pieces are structurally exact lower-bound contributions). The principled route to the actual A>=5 links remains the R5-full SDP canonical knot-ID (conj:canonical-knot-id-sdp, #604), which must first resolve its own A<=3 anchor non-confirmation. Nothing wired; no fit; every use of Vol4=8.048 is conditional/AME-implied.",
